WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:07.160
Here's a super easy question for you: Why
does Zoro want to become the strongest swordsman

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.160
in the world?

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.740
As a loyal one piece fan this should be pretty
easy to answer for you, right?

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:13.880
Or...is it really?

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:19.210
See, I recently asked myself the very same
thing and just like you right now was shocked

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:26.339
to find out that we actually have no idea
what Zoro's main motivation for his big dream

00:00:26.339 --> 00:00:28.320
ACTUALLY - IS.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:34.550
We know it for all the other straw hats.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:38.360
Sanji wants to find the all blue BECAUSE he
loves cooking.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:43.630
Robin wants to learn the true history BECAUSE
she wants to honor the sacrifice of Ohara

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.760
and take down the world government.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:51.640
Chopper wants to become a great doctor, BECAUSE
he wants to help even the sickest people.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.990
The only two people where neither you nor
me have any idea what their true motivation

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:05.860
is are, Luffy and...yeah Zoro, the two most
popular characters of the series.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:11.560
Luffy wants to become pirate king, but Oda
purposefully doesn't tell us his reason for

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.560
it.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.499
And Zoro of course wants to become the worlds
strongest swordsman, because, yeah because

00:01:17.499 --> 00:01:18.950
why exactly?

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:24.930
I hope you agree that it's probably not because
he needs to stroke stroke his own ego.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:31.240
And while Kuina was undoubtedly a big catalyst
for his growth, he wanted to become the strongest

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.840
even before meeting her.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:45.700
So, what is it, that drives Zoro to put his
life on the line over and over again for this

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.700
goal.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.909
And you're in luck, cause I think I managed
to find the key to fully unlocking Zoro's

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:58.359
character, by doing a complete socratic deep-dive
into his character, as deep as no-one has

00:01:58.359 --> 00:02:00.799
ever done before, probably.

00:02:00.799 --> 00:02:05.500
And let me tell you in advance, I think you
will be surprised by who Zoro really is and

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.740
what he knew all along.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:10.860
But be warned, this video WILL contain some
manga spoilers.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:17.000
Okay, so I have to shamelessly disclose here,
that Zoro is my favorite character and that

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:23.610
the original idea for this video was finding
out what made Zoro so incredibly likable and

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.610
popular.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:29.810
Only by doing that research did I accidentally
stumble onto the mystery behind his character.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:32.490
So allow me to guide you through my thought-process
here.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:38.080
If I held you at gunpoint to tell me what
makes Zoro so likable you'd probably say something

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.080
like this.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.080
Yo, tell me right now.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.080
And no games.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.080
Why do like Zoro.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.080
Who- who are you?

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.080
You like a Sanji fan or something.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.080
What did you call me?

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:46.080
Nothing.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.080
Why do like Zoro?

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.080
Oh jeez, I dunno.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.970
He's badass.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:50.970
Uhu.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.800
Go on.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:53.800
Swords?

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.640
Nice okay.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.010
Something like that.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.890
Zoro is a true badass.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.330
No question.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:06.000
But there are clearly many other characters
that fit the stoic, cool warrior trope, that

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.560
are not as popular as Zoro.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.070
So I figured there must be SOMETHING - MORE
to it.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:17.250
Something I really can relate to, that speaks
to me on a fundamental level.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:22.980
However, instead of trying to analyze Zoro,
I decided to flip this on its head and start

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:27.270
with the audience, myself.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:33.210
One of my biggest insecurities is that I personally
sometimes feel pretty lost in this vast and

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.920
rapidly-changing modern world that we live
in.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.780
Now I asked myself: what's the deeper truth
behind that.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:44.610
Well I guess it's that I don't have a clear
path in life.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.450
And the deeper truth behind that?

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:51.290
Is that I sometimes feel like I can't do anything.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:56.710
Going deeper, that means I sometimes don't
have confidence in myself.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:01.801
Meaning that I think that I'm not strong or
capable enough to change and influence the

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:04.220
things I want to change.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:10.340
Going one level deeper again, the meaning
behind this is that I am of no use to anyone.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.520
It means I don't deserve attention.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:18.139
And the truth beneath this is of course, that
I do want attention and purpose.

00:04:18.139 --> 00:04:19.139
In other words, I feel alone.

00:04:19.139 --> 00:04:23.010
Now if you like Zoro as well, I think you
might be able to relate to this break down

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.420
I just did of myself.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:31.790
Because as it turns out Zoro is a character
that has a clear answer to each and every

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.500
one of these questions.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:38.950
Even though he GETS lost a lot, he doesn't
FEEL lost.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:43.700
Just the opposite, he has a very clear place
in the world, fighting next to Luffy.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.960
He also has a clear path.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:50.270
He wants to become the strongest swordsman,
no matter what.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:56.960
And because he has centered his entire existence
around this goal, he is actually strong.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.740
Strong enough to change things.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.990
That means Zoro is confident in his skills
and in his ability to always improve.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.760
He knows he's strong and that he can help
others.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.139
And so Zoro is of use to those he cares about.

00:05:11.139 --> 00:05:15.720
As a result he deserves the positive attention
of the the people around him, friends and

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.710
foes alike, who respect him for his path.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.870
But Zoro doesn't need this attention in the
first place.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:31.260
He is okay being alone, but even more importantly,
he now has people around him that genuinely

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:39.210
care for him.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:44.590
If you share my fundamental insecurities,
Zoro is like the cure to that.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:49.710
He's not relatable, as much as he is an inspiration
and role model for me.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:55.360
Someone who fits the archetype of the true
hero, an ideal man that is very easy to look

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:01.120
up to and be inspired by, especially for guys
but for many girls as well.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:06.860
He's like a Japanese version of Hercules:
The silent, but gentle warrior, that follows

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:12.491
the way of the samurai, to defend those who
need him and who never leaves his path, even

00:06:12.491 --> 00:06:14.480
when faced with death.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:19.010
Except if its a literal path, then you can
be damn sure Zoro will leave that shit faster

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:21.200
than you can say Onigiri.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:29.970
And what I realized in this moment, is that
this is also the root cause for all the conflict

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:33.639
between people who like Sanji and people who
like Zoro.

00:06:33.639 --> 00:06:38.220
I love Sanji because he is relatable.

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:43.380
He arguably is the character with the most
human and emotional character development

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.430
in all of one piece.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:56.500
Sanji is all about growing as a person and
facing his insecurities.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:01.860
Zoro on the other hand is not really relatable,
but an ideal to strive towards.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:06.889
And while some people prefer to suffer with
Sanji and empathize with his journey, others

00:07:06.889 --> 00:07:17.500
prefer seeing an idealized, but unrealistic
version of what they want to become.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.310
And that makes sense.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:26.449
Zoro's arc so far in the story has been very
focused on getting stronger physically.

00:07:26.449 --> 00:07:32.389
Otherwise he has been the very disciplined,
kind-hearted and loyal person he is right

00:07:32.389 --> 00:07:35.860
from the very first chapter we meet him.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:40.949
Now I DO think that Oda has given him a little
bit of a personal arc as well, where being

00:07:40.949 --> 00:07:45.710
with Luffy and the other straw hats has made
him ease up a bit more and show more of a

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:51.700
human side, which is why we all love the rare
scenes Zoro laughs or has a human moment with

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.580
some other crew member.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:08:06.800
But overall, he is already a close to complete
character the moment he joins Luffy.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:13.350
And that brings me back to the original question:
Why does Zoro want to become the strongest

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:14.350
swordsman?

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:20.050
Now, I think it's absolutely plausible, that
this is all Oda ever wanted to do with Zoro.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:25.070
Have him be the perfect greek-god type of
character, that is easy to look up to.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:28.050
Which many many people already do, me included.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:34.930
So, you could definitely argue that Zoro doesn't
need any deeper motivation or a stronger theme

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:36.760
than he already has.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:41.630
But the recent developments in Wano have been
challenging that perspective drastically for

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:42.630
me.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:47.070
And I want to convince you that there is a
much more to Roronoa Zoro than you previously

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:48.070
thought.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.320
But first: Ad Break.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.800
Real quick I want to talk about Skillshare,
