00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:39.920
Just like many of the other straw hats, Zoro
didn't join Luffy because he wanted to become

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:45.420
a pirate, but because Luffy offered them the
chance to reach their goal.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.040
And why does he have that goal?

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:51.810
Well, thinking about that question, made it
painfully clear to me, that we actually don't

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:55.420
know Zoro all that well, when you think about
it.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:10:00.380
He doesn't talk much in general and the moments
where he shares something about himself are

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:02.270
very very rare.

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:08.160
So, I thought to myself: Let's try the same
deconstruction technique I just used on myself,

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:16.740
but this time with Zoro.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:20.670
We know for a fact that Zoro wants to become
the strongest swordsman.

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:23.980
So what's the deeper truth behind that?

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:26.360
Is it because he wants attention?

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:29.300
Because he needs people to stroke his ego?

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:33.490
You know just as well as me, that that's not
what Zoro is about at all.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:38.950
So there must be some other deeper meaning
behind it.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:43.830
The idea behind that dream is basically: I
want to be the strongest.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:49.420
Swordsmanship is simply the way Zoro grew
up with, given that he has roots in Wano,

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:51.270
which has now been pretty much confirmed.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:11:08.470
So swords are just Zoro's way to become strong,
just as his devil fruit is for Luffy.

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:13.959
Now being the strongest means that Zoro wants
to be stronger than anyone else.

00:11:13.959 --> 00:11:18.500
The deeper meaning behind that is that he
wants to be able to do what he wants or needs

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:19.500
to.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:25.360
There is something he wants to change or defend
or take back that he only can do if he is

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.290
stronger than anyone else.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:32.880
And given all the hints we have gotten to
Zoro's connection to Wano and the Shimotsuki

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:41.959
family, I strongly believe that Zoro's real
goal is and always has been - to free Wano.

00:11:41.959 --> 00:11:48.750
I'm gonna give you a second to process that
and what better way to do that then by subscribing

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.620
to the channel.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:58.670
Now, I totally understand that at first it
sounds strange that Zoro wanted to free Wano

00:11:58.670 --> 00:11:59.790
all this time.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:02.240
After all he never mentioned it before.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:08.170
But has he ever mentioned ANYTHING really
about his personal history or goal, like ever?

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:14.060
No, I think that Zoro, just like Robin, is
a member of the straw hat crew, that knows

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:18.220
much much more about the world, than they
let on.

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:19.220
Think about it.

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:21.250
Doesn't it make all the sense in the world.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:25.970
No matter if Zoro was born in Wano or simply
was told of his home after being born in the

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:42.430
east blue, he grew up with the knowledge that
Orochi and Kaido were tyrannizing his country.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:47.730
Zoro being related to the Shimotsuke family,
that Ryuuma is also a part of, makes it very

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:53.510
likely that he would have a very deep emotional
connection to the place, despite growing up

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:54.510
in the east blue.

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:58.390
The Dojo where he met Kuina is also heavily
connected to Wano.

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:14.050
And seeing his resemblance to the Daimyo of
Ringo, of course they wanted to keep him there.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:22.140
So for the sake of argument, let's just assume
for a second that this is actually true and

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:26.620
Zoro wants to free Wano despite never having
been there.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:27.620
So.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:28.620
much of the story.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:29.620
suddenly.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:30.620
makes.

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:31.620
sense.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:35.710
Of course he'd want to become the strongest
swordsman if his goal was taking out Kaido

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:36.860
and Orochi.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:43.529
Zoro joins Luffy because he sees in him a
chance to get closer to Wano and his goal.

00:13:43.529 --> 00:13:48.769
Throughout the story HE is the most serious
about their journey and Luffy being a good

00:13:48.769 --> 00:13:53.730
captain, because HE has the highest stakes
in them actually making it to the new world

00:13:53.730 --> 00:14:03.420
and Wano, knowing right from the start what
sort of beast they are up against.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:08.680
Seeing how far he is from Mihawk at the Baratie,
I even made a whole video about it, shows

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:14.470
Zoro that he is not even close to beating
the man who might just barely have a chance

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:15.650
against Kaido.

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:17.660
And let me blow your mind about something
else.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:23.960
The scene on thriller bark, where Zoro sacrifices
himself for Luffy, is one of the most famous

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.550
in the story, something I made a video about
as well.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:32.029
Generally, people tend to take Zoro's sacrifice
here to mean that Luffy's dream is more important

00:14:32.029 --> 00:14:33.560
than his own.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:44.269
Same when he asks Mihawk to train him for
Luffy's sake, throwing away his honor.

00:14:44.269 --> 00:14:50.040
But when you look at it through the Wano lens,
Zoro KNOWS that Luffy is the person who will

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:54.420
have the best chance at taking on the likes
of Kaido and Orochi.

00:14:54.420 --> 00:15:00.680
He is convinced that Luffy is the one who
can free Wano and change the world.

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:06.329
It's not that he is willing to give up his
dream in exchange for Luffy's, he inherits

00:15:06.329 --> 00:15:10.210
his will to liberate Wano TO LUFFY to carry
it on.

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:14.810
Similarly, how does Zoro know that Ryuma is
from Wano?

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:27.460
Zoro is fully aware of what Wano is like,
all along.

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:32.630
When they receive the SOS call form Punk hazard
about a samurai, Zoro immediately mentions

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:36.080
it to Brook, who is the one who explains it
to us.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:39.310
But Zoro knows.

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:43.960
When they pick up Momo and Kinemon on their
way to Dressrosa and Law explains Doflamingo's

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:49.720
connection to Kaido, we see the famous dots
from Zoro.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:54.940
And what I found really interesting is that
Oda did not show us any of Zoro's reaction

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:58.110
to all the Wano-related reveals on Zou.

00:15:58.110 --> 00:16:03.860
The only time we see his face is when Kinemon
and Momo reveal that Oden had been killed

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.240
by Kaido.

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:08.430
Literally everyone is shocked, except Zoro.

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:10.670
He just looks more determined.

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:23.130
And then of course, we have Zoro in Wano,
being like a fish in the water.

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:36.370
Basically, all moments with Zoro fit really
nicely into the idea that this is the place

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:40.800
he wanted to come to all along, but I want
to pick out a few scenes in particular.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:45.459
For one we have the entire plot-line between
him and Hiyori.

00:16:45.459 --> 00:16:50.070
Seeing Orochi's execution of Yasuie, he goes
for Orochi's head right away.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:55.820
If he had grown up with the sole goal of killing
this man, and then seeing his cruelty in action

00:16:55.820 --> 00:17:02.120
for the first time himself, of course he wouldn't
be able to hold back and go right for his

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.120
head.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:07.980
Now, I agree that Zoro also always wanted
to take down Kaido, but he has decided long

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:13.959
ago, that he will leave Kaido to Luffy if
necessary, just as it happened in the Manga.

00:17:13.959 --> 00:17:17.820
Orochi on the other hand I'm convinced will
fall to Zoro's hand.

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:22.760
This scene here with Hiyori basically confirms
this and I'm pretty sure it's Zoro talking

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:24.699
here all the way.

00:17:24.699 --> 00:17:29.490
This would also fit in really nicely with
the Japanese legend of Orochi, who was slain

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:34.810
by the wind-god Susanoo by getting the snake
drunk on sake and then killing it with the

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:39.210
sword Ame-no-habakiri, the sister sword of
Enma in One Piece.

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:44.410
Zoro loving sake, having been shown a certain
affinity to wind-style attacks and a close

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:49.690
relation to Shinto-buddhism overall.

00:17:49.690 --> 00:18:01.000
Once again, Zoro willingly is putting his
life on the line just to keep fighting, drinking

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.200
the special medicine of the minks.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:07.760
As he says in the panel here: All that matters,
is being able to fight right now.

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:10.720
He can't leave this one to Luffy alone.

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:16.230
It's what he trained for his entire life and
he has to do everything he can possibly do

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:19.030
to see this battle through.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:23.273
When Kaido told the scabbards that Wano will
never see a monster samurai of Oden's like

00:18:23.273 --> 00:18:30.970
again, it only takes a few chapters, until
Zoro is called the mirrored image of Ryuuma,

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:33.970
the most legendary Samurai of them all.

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:39.610
Zoro says he will have all the samurai of
Wano follow him in no time, and indeed he

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:43.549
is a true king, being able to use conqueror's
haki.

00:18:43.549 --> 00:18:48.549
I'm convinced that very soon we will get a
lot of reveals surrounding Zoro's origin,

00:18:48.549 --> 00:18:54.570
and based on what I just told you, I'm pretty
sure that Zoro knew way more about his and

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:58.540
Wano's past than Oda let us on to believe.

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:03.690
If you truly want to understand Zoro's character
however, you really have to watch my analysis

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:06.909
of him here, next.

